#basePath P3_LampreyDownstream
#include "Header.leaf"

:: Start
@exposed
@cutscene

// Mark start of thread
$set global:currentThread = "P3_LampreyDownstream"


// Splits dialogue depending on which option player chose first
$if global:upstreamFirst == false
       {@Claire}   
              Sea lamprey go downstream as soon as they have matured to feed on fish!
              Which means that any intervention focusing on sea lamprey going downstream is meant to stop them from getting to the lake!

       {@You}
              So that they would never feed on the other fish in the first place! That makes a lot of sense, Claire.

       {@Claire}
              Why thank you, young scientist!
       $call GiveEvidenceChip("Evidence-Feed-Downstream")

       {@Claire}
              If you have any other questions, I'm happy to answer them, but I know you can be quite busy!

       {@You}
              Let's see...
       $set global:downstreamFirst = true

$elseif global:upstreamFirst == true
       {@Claire}   
              Sea lamprey go downstream as soon as they have matured to feed on fish!
              Which means that any intervention focusing on sea lamprey going downstream is meant to stop them from getting to the lake!

       {@You}
              So that they would never feed on the other fish in the first place! That makes a lot of sense, Claire.

       {@Claire}
              Why thank you, young scientist!
       $call GiveEvidenceChip("Evidence-Feed-Downstream")

       {@Claire}
              Well, my work here is done! Shall we go into town for a dessert?

       {@You}
              I can't, but maybe this weekend?

       {@Claire}
              We have a deal. 

       {@}
              She walks with you back to your car.
$endif
// TODO: Rest of thread here

$call UnlockLocation(DNROffice)    // .AtDNROffice
$call SetTravelTime(DNROffice, 1)
$call SetNextAssetAtLocation(DNROffice, "Evidence-repellent-traps")
$call EnableMapButton()
$call CheckIfOutOfTime()
$call OpenMap()


:: AtDNROffice
@trigger    OnLocationChanged
// global:currentThread ensures the correct thread
// global:currentPhase == 3 ensures player is in phase 3
@when       global:currentThread == "P3_LampreyDownstream", global:currentPhase == 3, location == "DNROffice"
// Lock all location on map
$call SetInThreadLocks()
$call DisableMapButton()
$call SetBackground("bg/dnr-office-bg.png")


// Splits dialogue depending on whether the player has been to the DNR before
$if global:dnrVisited = false
       {@}   
              Paul is jamming to something when you step into the DNR office. He's hiding it well, but you can see it in his eyes. 

       {@You}
              What're you working on?

       {@}
              He nearly jumps out of his seat.

       {@Paul}
              Ah. Well, I guess the cat is out of the bag. I moonlight as a DJ.

       {@You}
              You? DJ?

       {@Paul}
              Mmm. Yes. So what can I help you with?

       {@You}
              I'm working on preparing interventions targeting sea lamprey going downstream. Has the DNR worked on those before?

       {@Paul}
              Mm, yes, certainly. Back when we had more traps, we would place some to catch sea lamprey heading to the lake.

       $if !HasSeen(P3_Sterile.End) //references sterilization if the player has already seen it
              {@Paul}
                     Those were the sea lamprey that would then be sent to be sterilized, back when we did that en masse. 
       $endif

       {@You}
              Could these programs with traps be restarted?

       {@Paul}
              Mm. Yes, but you would have to talk to the Army Corps of Engineers about it. They are responsible for that. 
       $call GiveEvidenceChip("Evidence-repellent-traps")

       {@You}
              Perfect! Sounds like a plan. 

       {@Paul}
              Mm, yes. Have a great day. 

       {@}
              You're on your way out when you feel the need to turn around and yell-

       {@You}
              Oh, and Paul?
              Good luck tonight, Mr. DJ!

       {@}
              His quiet grumble sounds more pleased than usual.
       $set global:dnrVisited = true

$else
       {@}
              Paul has his headphones on again, but when you step in he gives you a private smile.

       {@You}
              How's the set going, Mr. DJ?

       {@Paul}
              Mm. I'd say I'm on to something. Is there anything else you need from me?

       {@You}
              There is, yeah. I was wondering if the DNR worked on any interventions targeting sea lamprey going downstream. 
              Maybe like those traps we talked about earlier?

       {@Paul}
              Mm. Yes, we have done that before. Though just like with upstream traps, you'll need to talk to Corps.

       {@You}
              That can definitely be arranged. Thanks for your help, Paul.

       {@Paul}
              Of course.
              Mmmm. Come to my performance tonight. 

       {@You}
              Really? I'd love to.

       {@Paul}
              Mm. Yes. No point in DJing if no one listens.

       {@You}
              Well, I guess I have to come, then. 
$endif
// TODO: Rest of DNR Office section here

// TODO: Give evidence chip
$call GiveEvidenceChip("Evidence-repellent-traps")

$call UnlockLocation(ArmyCorps)    // .AtArmyCorps
$call SetTravelTime(ArmyCorps, 1)
$call SetNextAssetAtLocation(ArmyCorps, "Action-downstream-tributary-traps")
$call EnableMapButton()
$call CheckIfOutOfTime()
$call OpenMap()


:: AtArmyCorps
@trigger    OnLocationChanged
// global:currentThread ensures the correct thread
// global:currentPhase == 3 ensures player is in phase 3
@when       global:currentThread == "P3_LampreyDownstream", global:currentPhase == 3, location == "ArmyCorps"
// Lock all location on map
$call SetInThreadLocks()
$call DisableMapButton()
$call SetBackground("bg/army-corps-bg.png")


//Splits dialogue depending on whether the player has previously been to the Army Corps
$if global:corpsVisited = false
       {@}   
              Robertson is deep in work on a trap but turns to greet you as you step out of the car.

       {@Robertson}
              It's mighty good to see you again, ma'am. So, what can I help you with?

       {@You}
              I've been talking to Paul down at the DNR, and we're thinking of putting in new traps for sea lamprey going downstream.
              Would you be able to make and place those traps for us?

       {@Robertson}
              Oh, certainly, ma'am. We'd be very pleased to help. Just let us know whenever you need 'em.
       $call GiveActionCard("Action-downstream-tributary-traps")

       $if StatCheck(Research, 3)
              $if HasActionCard()
                     // handle player already has action card from LampreyUpstream thread
              $else
                     {@You}
                            Well, if we're putting traps facing one direction, why not put it in the other?
                            Claire told me that sea lamprey go upstream to spawn. So if we put traps going upstream, we can keep the sea lamprey from reproducing!
                     
                     {@Robertson}
                            Yes, ma'am, we can definitely do that.
                     $call GiveActionCard("Action-upstream-tributary-traps")

                     {@You}
                            Oh, I'm a genius, Robertson! Thank you, thank you!
                     {@Robertson}
                            I think that one was all you, ma'am.

              $endif
       $endif
       {@You}
              Thank you so much, Robertson. 

       {@Robertson}
              'Course. Anytime. 
       $set global:corpsVisited = true

$elseif global:corpsVisited = true
       {@}
              Robertson seems to have already begun preparation on those traps. 

       {@You}
              Heya. I'm back.

       {@Robertson}
              Nice to see ya so soon. Anything else needed?

       {@You}
              Yup. So you know how we're doing traps for sea lamprey going upstream?
              Well, I've talked to Paul, and we've decided that it could be worth doing them for sea lamprey going downstream, too.

       {@Robertson}
              Sounds like a mighty fine idea to me. Just let us know when you need 'em, and we'll have 'em.
       $call GiveActionCard("Action-downstream-tributary-traps")

       {@You}
              Thank you, Robertson! You're the best.

       {@Robertson}
              Aw, shucks. You flatter me, ma'am.
              By the way, I've heard someone over at the university is looking at ways to make traps more effective. Might be worth yer time.

       {@You}
              Interesting. I think I might know who that is...
$endif

// TODO: Give action card IF High research (traps on upstream)
// this has been moved up

// skip to end
$goto .End


:: End
@exposed
@tracked

// Mark end of thread
$set global:currentThread = "NONE"

// Go to Phase 2 Continue Hub
$goto P3_Hub.Continue